If a patient is an older-adult and the patient receives an opioid-therapy then every clinician should implement a common-opioid-risk-mitigation-intervention for the patient.
If a patient is an older-adult and the patient receives an opioid-therapy then every clinician may recommend an exercise-regimen to the patient for a constipation-prevention.
If a patient is an older-adult and the patient receives an opioid-therapy then every clinician may use a bowel-regimen for the patient for a constipation-prevention.
A common-opioid-risk-mitigation-intervention-example includes a constipation-prevention-intervention-example and includes a fall-risk-assessment-example and includes a cognitive-impairment-monitoring-example.
